<TeXmacs|2.1.4>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Data formats, converters and databases>

  These chapters describe how <TeXmacs> exchanges documents with the
  outside world and how it stores structured data. The first one presents
  the general converter machinery (data formats, the converter graph and
  converter options) and the individual converters; the second one goes into
  the details of the <LaTeX> and <name|HTML> converters, which are the most
  complex ones; the third one describes the embedded database engine, used
  among other things for bibliographies.

  The user level view is given in <hlink|compatibility with other
  formats|../../main/convert/man-convert.en.tm>.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|Converters to other data formats|conversions.en.tm>

    <branch|The <LaTeX> and <name|HTML> converters|convert.en.tm>

    <branch|The database and bibliographies|database.en.tm>

    <branch|The BibTeX engine and bibliography styles|bibtex.en.tm>
  </traverse>

